cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MeshBench
message: >-
  If you use MeshBench for published work, please cite it — and please say
  which RF mode produced your numbers, because the two carry different error
  budgets.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alex
    email: meshbench@pm.me
repository-code: https://github.com/MeshBench/meshbench
abstract: >-
  An RF-accurate MeshCore network simulator. It runs real MeshCore firmware
  against a sample-accurate LoRa baseband channel with real noise, so the
  question it answers is not whether a packet would get through but what
  arrived at the antenna, and why. Reception is decided by a full receive
  chain — demodulation, Gray mapping, the diagonal deinterleaver, Hamming FEC,
  dewhitening, header and payload CRC — so capture effect and partial overlap
  emerge rather than being ruled on. Known limits, and the direction each one
  errs in, are published in docs/shortcomings.md.
keywords:
  - LoRa
  - MeshCore
  - radio propagation
  - network simulation
  - software-defined radio
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
